    "description": "A MEDAS 2.0 (pre-release) project update: the dev backend on Cloud Run returned Service Unavailable on every request, including /health. Traced through Cloud Run logs to a stale MONGODB_URI secret pointing at a terminated cluster; because init_database() runs at import time, the failed connection crashed every worker boot. Fixed with a new dev Atlas cluster under the institutional account, a new secret version picked up via :latest, and verified with /health plus a real login query.",
    "note": "Evidence handling: the dev database holds example test data only, no real patient data. Log shown in B12 is sanitized (client IP, instance ID, trace/span IDs, project ID and full service URLs removed). B04/B06 are reconstructions from the incident notes, labeled as such on screen; B08 is a labeled illustration of the pattern, not MEDAS source. Dev URLs returning 503 since 2026-09-20 is a separate billing issue and is not part of this story.",
