    {
      "beat_id": "B08",
      "act": "WHY IT WAS TOTAL",
      "role_note": "labeled illustration of the import-time pattern, not MEDAS source",
      "narration_text": "Why did one bad setting take down everything, even the health check? Because init database runs at module import time, before Flask can serve a single request. The failed connection doesn't break one route. It breaks the boot. No healthy worker means no response at all, and Cloud Run just tries again on the next request.",
